Revision history for the tg skill

2.41  2026-09-18
      - IMPROVEMENT (TGT-303, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep, the final ticket of this sweep):
        cli/tts.pl also skips the mandatory --db/-d/D2TG_DB guard
        (matching cli/help.pl's own precedent) but never explained why
        in its own POD. Added a DESCRIPTION paragraph stating the
        guard doesn't apply since this command touches no state,
        network beyond the TTS engine, or credentials at all.

2.40  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-302, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): cli/history.pl's --since/--until shape
        regex accepted syntactically well-formed but calendrically
        invalid dates (e.g. 2026-13-45, 2026-02-30, a non-leap-year
        2026-02-29) - the shape check never confirmed the value was a
        real calendar date, only that it looked date-shaped. Added a
        round-trip validation via core Time::Piece (which silently
        rolls an out-of-range date forward rather than dying, so the
        parsed value is compared back against the original) after the
        existing shape check.

2.39  2026-09-18
      - IMPROVEMENT (TGT-301, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): cli/send.pl's own --db validation
        computed base_dir but never used it - the script never opens
        a Store and never touches attachments_dir. Removed the unused
        variable assignment, kept the validation call itself (a real
        side effect - it requires the alias to resolve to an existing
        directory), and added an explicit comment stating why.

2.38  2026-09-18
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-300, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): extracted embedded POD from 6 modules
        (Download.pm, Lock.pm, Subprocess.pm, TTS.pm, Poller/Format.pm,
        Store/RetryQueue.pm) into matching .pod files, matching the
        rest of the codebase's established convention. Fixed 4 files'
        worth of pre-existing bare-name L<> link errors this surfaced
        once t/277-podchecker-clean.t started checking them. Also
        self-caught and corrected a real mistake from TGT-296/298: both
        had wrongly added new embedded POD to Config/Paths.pm and
        Store/Schema.pm despite each already having its own separate
        .pod file - moved that content to the correct existing files.
        Zero functional code change; 100% coverage confirmed on all 8
        touched modules.

2.37  2026-09-18
      - IMPROVEMENT (TGT-299, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): D2TG::Lock::acquire's "last one wins"
        SIGKILL takeover path had an undocumented PID-reuse race
        between its liveness check and its kill. Explicitly documented
        this accepted risk in acquire()'s own POD, matching
        find_other_pollers' own established documented-risk precedent
        - no code behavior change.

2.36  2026-09-18
      - IMPROVEMENT (TGT-298, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): added 2 idempotent indexes,
        idx_messages_read_at and idx_messages_created_at, so an
        unscoped unread_messages or a wide --since/--until history
        query no longer requires a full table scan as message volume
        grows. Additive migration, safe on both fresh and existing
        databases.

2.35  2026-09-18
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-297, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): D2TG::Store::AccessControl.pm's
        is_allowed/add_pending/approve/seed_admin used positional-
        argument bot_key scoping, unlike every sibling Store submodule
        extracted in the same TGT-278/279 pass (History,
        SentReplyAudit, RetryQueue), which use %args-style. Converted
        AccessControl.pm's 4 functions to %args-style and updated
        D2TG::Store.pm's own 5 direct call sites into it - D2TG::Store's
        own public forwarding API (used by every existing caller)
        stays positional and unchanged. 100% statement+subroutine
        coverage confirmed on both touched modules.

2.34  2026-09-18
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-296, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): D2TG::Config::Paths.pm's 4 path
        resolvers (state_db_path, attachments_dir, lock_path,
        heartbeat_path) each duplicated identical base_dir/.tira
        resolution logic. Collapsed onto one shared private helper
        (_resolve_state_path) - zero observable behavior change, 100%
        statement+subroutine coverage confirmed.

2.33  2026-09-18
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-295, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): D2TG::Store::RetryQueue.pm's download
        and transcription sides were byte-for-byte twins differing
        only by table name - record_failed_download/
        record_failed_transcription, failed_downloads/
        failed_transcriptions, failed_downloads_due_for_retry/
        failed_transcriptions_due_for_retry,
        mark_failed_download_retried/mark_failed_transcription_retried,
        remove_failed_download/remove_failed_transcription. Collapsed
        each pair onto one table-parameterized private helper
        (_record_failed, _list_failed, _due_for_retry, _mark_retried,
        _remove_failed) - zero observable behavior change, 100%
        statement+subroutine coverage confirmed.

2.32  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-294, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): docs/commands.md and lib/D2TG/Poller.pod
        both referred to D2TG::Poller::_print_reply_template as the
        poller's REPLY WITH template function - renamed and relocated
        during the TGT-259/TGT-276 decomposition to
        D2TG::Poller::Format::print_reply_template. Anyone grepping the
        codebase for the documented name found nothing. The same stale
        name also appeared in 3 comments inside currently-passing tests
        (t/217, t/220, t/226). Corrected all 5 references.

2.31  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-293, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): 14 $store-> method calls across 7 cli
        scripts (history.pl, retry-download.pl, retry-transcription.pl,
        attachment.pl, unread.pl, reply.pl, text-only-replies.pl) ran
        completely unwrapped by eval. D2TG::Store->new sets
        RaiseError => 1, and D2TG::Poller::Safe::open_store_or_die only
        wraps the constructor call itself - a locked/busy SQLite
        database at any of these 14 call sites raw-crashed with an
        uncaught DBI exception (which can embed the real db path)
        instead of this project's own established clean-refusal
        convention. Only cli/approve.pl's own $store-> calls were
        already correctly wrapped. All 14 sites now eval-wrapped and
        classified via D2TG::Poller::Safe::classify_store_error,
        matching the pattern TGT-183/186/195 already established for
        other call sites.

2.30  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-292, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): 5 stale POD L<> cross-references left
        over from the TGT-263/265 module moves (cli/reply.pl,
        cli/retry-download.pl, cli/approve.pl,
        cli/retry-transcription.pl, lib/D2TG/Store.pod) pointed at
        functions in their old, pre-move locations. t/266's own
        regression test - written specifically to catch this class of
        drift - never actually matched the L<Module/name> POD link
        syntax these files use, only the fully-qualified Module::name
        call syntax, so the staleness sat undetected. Fixed all 5
        links and widened t/266's own regex to catch both syntaxes.

2.29  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-291, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): is_transient_error's 5xx regex never
        got the same \b word-boundary anchor its 429 sibling has - a
        near-miss like "status 5001" was incorrectly matched and
        classified as transient. Added the anchor, matching the 429
        check's own established pattern exactly.

2.28  2026-09-18
      - BUGFIX (TGT-290, found via a user-requested comprehensive
        bug/improvement sweep): the shared multipart boundary generator
        used by send_voice/send_photo/send_document had only ~30 bits
        of entropy ('D2TGBoundary' . int(rand(1e9)) . time). A file
        whose raw bytes happened to contain the generated boundary
        string would corrupt the upload request. Replaced with
        _generate_boundary, using 8 rounds of rand(65536) for 128 bits
        of real entropy - fixes all 3 upload paths in one place. No
        behavior change beyond the boundary string's own composition.

2.27  2026-09-17
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-288, found via a scheduled JOB-004 improvement
        hunt following up on TGT-287): 7 test files deliberately read
        another package's variable/sub by full qualification exactly
        once (to keep a doc-accuracy assertion derived from the real
        constant instead of a re-typed literal) - Perl's strict-vars
        warning system flagged each as "used only once: possible
        typo", cluttering every full-suite run with real-but-benign
        noise. Scoped `no warnings 'once'` added around each offending
        reference; no assertion logic changed.

2.26  2026-09-17
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-287, found via a scheduled JOB-003/004 sweep
        following up on TGT-286): the 2-line resolve_alias_dir_or_die
        + require_existing_base_dir_or_die pairing was hand-copied,
        byte-for-byte, across 12 cli/*.pl scripts (approve, attachment,
        history, poller, reply, retry-download, retry-transcription,
        send, status, text-only-replies, unread, whoami) - the same
        duplication class TGT-203/230/269 already removed at the
