        base_dir_or_die composing both calls; all 12 sites now use it.
        Zero behavior change. Also extracted D2TG::Config::Paths.pm's
        own embedded POD (previously inline after __END__) to a new
        Paths.pod, matching established convention, since this ticket
        substantively touched that module.

2.25  2026-09-17
      - BUGFIX (TGT-286, found via a scheduled JOB-003 hourly bug hunt):
        cli/poller.pl's two D2TG::Config::Flags::bot_groups calls (the
        validation-only pass and the real one) were the only startup
        failure paths in this script never brought into the
        TGT-183/184/185 clean-refusal convention - a malformed
        --chat_id shape, a duplicate (chat_id, bot token) pair, or a
        bot token reused across chat ids used to surface as a raw,
        uncaught Perl exception instead of the script's own "... -
        refusing to start." STDERR shape. Both calls now go through a
        new bot_groups_or_die wrapper that strips the module-qualified
        prefix and refuses cleanly, matching every other failure path.
        No behavior change to exit codes or which inputs are accepted -
        only the STDERR message shape for the already-refused cases.

2.24  2026-09-17
