        files, 2344 tests) and 100% coverage confirmed unchanged.

2.21  2026-09-17
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-278, found via a wc -l sweep run as TGT-277's
        own pipeline-continuity backlog check): D2TG::Store.pm was 1378
        lines - by far the largest module in the codebase, over 2.7x
        the board's 500-line-per-module cap, and never previously
        audited despite this session's extensive module-decomposition
        history covering every other large module. Surveyed its own
        function clusters and extracted the largest cohesive one -
        message history (record_message/get_message/
        get_attachment_path/mark_read/is_read/unread_messages/
        recent_messages/messages_in_range, 8 functions) - into a new
        D2TG::Store::History module, mirroring D2TG::Store::RetryQueue's
        own established precedent: built once in D2TG::Store::new,
        thin forwarders kept for every existing caller, zero behavior
        change. Also extracted Store.pm's own embedded POD (never
        previously in a separate file) into Store.pod, and fixed 22
        podchecker unresolved-link errors found while doing so (2 in
        the newly-written History.pod, 20 pre-existing in the newly-
        extracted Store.pod - the same bare-name-vs-signature bug class
        TGT-277 just fixed elsewhere, never checked here since this
        module had no separate .pod file before). D2TG::Store.pm is
        now 720 lines - still over the cap but down from 1378; filed
        follow-up TGT-279 for the remaining 2 clusters (access control,
        sent-reply audit) plus D2TG::Telegram.pm's own smaller 547-line
        overage. New t/278-store-history-module.t proves the new
        module's ownership. Full Docker suite and 100% coverage on
        both D2TG::Store and D2TG::Store::History confirmed unchanged.

2.20  2026-09-17
      - DOC FIX (TGT-277, found via a podchecker sweep during TGT-276's
        own documentation work): 6 lib/**/*.pod files (Config.pod,
        Config/Flags.pod, Reply/Args.pod, Transcribe.pod,
        Transcribe/Retry.pod, Poller/Safe.pod) had 48 unresolved
        internal L<name> links, plus a UTF-8 encoding warning in
        Reply/Args.pod. Root cause in every case: a link targeted a
        bare function name while the matching =head2 anchor included
        the full signature (e.g. "=head2 extract_bot_flag(@args)" vs
        "L</extract_bot_flag>") - podchecker requires an exact match.
        Fixed by widening each link to L<name()|/exact anchor text>;
        added a leading "=encoding UTF-8" directive to Reply/Args.pod
        for its own literal non-ASCII mojibake example. New
        t/277-podchecker-clean.t runs Pod::Checker's own Perl API
        against every lib/**/*.pod file, asserting zero errors, so
        this drift class is now caught automatically. No code changed
        - full Docker suite passes unchanged.

2.19  2026-09-17
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-276, found via TGT-275's own REQ-029 audit):
        D2TG::Poller.pm was still 598 lines after TGT-275's own helper
        relocation, entirely due to run_once itself (~520 lines
        dispatching 3 branches: message_reaction, edited_message, and
        the plain-text/voice/media fallback). Splitting the branches
        into same-file functions would not have reduced the module's
        line count at all (nothing removed, only reorganized) - so,
        matching the D2TG::Poller::Safe/Format precedent, the 3
        branch handlers (plus their own extensive historical comments)
        were relocated into a new D2TG::Poller::Dispatch module.
        run_once itself is now a short dispatch loop. Every guard
        clause that used a bare "next" inside run_once's own loop
        became a "return" inside the extracted handler functions -
        next outside of a loop is a fatal runtime error, and a handler
        function has no loop of its own; run_once's own dispatch loop
        calls next unconditionally right after each handler returns.
        Also found and fixed a real documentation-accuracy bug left
        over from TGT-275: 5 function sections in Poller.pod (and 4
        stray commands.md/cli/poller.pl/Config.pod mentions) still
        described open_store_or_die/run_once_safe/store_write_safe/
        persist_offset_safe/skill_version_check_safe as if they still
        lived in D2TG::Poller, when TGT-275 had already moved them to
        D2TG::Poller::Safe - corrected all of them. Also removed 10 of
        D2TG::Poller's own 11 D2TG::Poller::Format forwarders as
        permanently-uncallable dead code (their only caller, run_once,
        moved to D2TG::Poller::Dispatch, which calls Format's bare
        functions directly) - only _bot_flag survives, for its one
        remaining external caller. New t/276-poller-dispatch-module.t
        proves the new module's ownership. Zero behavior change - full
        Docker suite and 100% coverage on both D2TG::Poller and
        D2TG::Poller::Dispatch confirmed unchanged. D2TG::Poller.pm is
        now 74 lines; D2TG::Poller::Dispatch.pm is 275 lines - both
        comfortably under the 500-line-per-module cap.

2.18  2026-09-17
      - MAINTENANCE (TGT-275, found via TGT-273's own REQ-029 audit):
        D2TG::Poller.pm was 854 lines after TGT-273's POD extraction -
        over this board's 500-line-per-module cap. The 8 non-run_once
        helper functions (open_store_or_die, run_once_safe,
        record_message_safe, record_message_and_track_offset,
        classify_store_error, store_write_safe, persist_offset_safe,
