1.36  2026-09-10
      - FEATURE (TGT-169, live Telegram question from Michael, msg
        #246): "is the implementable if the user on telegram edit the
        previous message and that will notify the agent about the
        updated message or notifiy the agent the message was deleted
        by user. is that something we can code for it?" Split answer:
        EDIT detection is now implemented - Telegram sends a distinct
        edited_message update (same shape as an ordinary message,
        reflecting the post-edit content) generally when a message
        known to the bot in an allow-listed chat is edited.
        D2TG::Telegram::get_updates now requests edited_message in its
        allowed_updates default alongside message/message_reaction -
        edited_message is not itself opt-in the way message_reaction
        is (Telegram's own baseline default already includes it; it
        only stopped reaching this project once TGT-143 first narrowed
        allowed_updates to a fixed list at all - and that baseline is
        historical, not a live fallback, since getUpdates retains a
        bot's last-set allowed_updates rather than reverting to the
        baseline if a later call omits the parameter). D2TG::Poller::run_once
        gained a new branch recognizing update.edited_message and
        printing a distinct "NEW TG EDIT [chat_id] sender: <new text>
        (msg #N, edited)" line, gated by the same is_allowed
        access-control check every other branch uses (no add_pending -
        an edit isn't a first-contact event, matching message_reaction's
        own precedent) - and recording a text edit's new content via
        record_message so d2 tg.history reflects it (a caption/media-
        only edit is announced but not recorded, to avoid overwriting
        an already-correct history summary with nothing useful - a
        Codex review finding). DELETE detection of an ordinary chat
        message remains impossible - the Bot API has no update type
        for it (a separate, business-connection-scoped
        deleted_business_messages update exists for an unrelated
        feature this project doesn't use), a hard platform limitation,
        not a gap in this skill's own implementation.

