1.34  2026-09-10
      - BUG FIX (TGT-166, found via a scheduled hourly bug hunt, a
        direct follow-up sweep after TGT-165 for the same unwrapped-
        DBI-call pattern): cli/poller.pl's persistent main loop called
        $store->set_offset(...) directly, with no eval wrapper. Unlike
        run_once's own is_allowed/add_pending calls (just fixed in
        TGT-165, both inside run_once_safe's own eval), this call sat
        at the TOP LEVEL of the persistent poller script's main loop -
        so a locked/busy SQLite database crashed the ENTIRE poller
        process outright, not just one poll cycle's batch. Since this
        process runs indefinitely under Tira's own monitor-job
        supervision, routine SQLite lock contention (the same risk
        TGT-129/TGT-132/TGT-165 already established as real and
        recurring) could silently take the whole poller offline until
        Tira's monitor-dead/monitor-silent policy noticed and someone
        restarted it - a strictly worse consequence than the batch-
        redelivery bug TGT-165 fixed, one call site over. Extracted
        into D2TG::Poller::persist_offset_safe (a new, directly unit-
        testable function): catches the error, classifies it into a
        short fixed reason (TGT-133 precedent - never echoes the raw
        exception, which can embed the database file's own path), logs
        it to STDERR, and returns - the poller keeps running and a
        later poll cycle attempts to persist its own (by then newer)
        offset again, not a retry of the specific failed value; if the
        process exits before a later persist succeeds, the previously
        persisted offset remains on disk and updates since then may be
        redelivered after a restart.
        get_offset (called once at startup) is unaffected, correctly
        still fatal - matches every other setup guard's own convention.

1.33  2026-09-10
      - BUG FIX (TGT-165, found via a scheduled hourly bug hunt):
        D2TG::Poller::run_once's is_allowed/add_pending calls (message_
        reaction branch and plain message branch) had no eval wrapper,
        unlike every record_message call site, which TGT-132 already
        wrapped for this exact reason. Both is_allowed and add_pending
        run against a RaiseError=>1 DBI handle, so a locked/busy
        SQLite database made either call die - unwrapped, that
        propagated uncaught out of run_once, aborting the whole poll
        batch. Since run_once_safe preserves the pre-batch offset on
        error, the ENTIRE batch - including already-printed updates -
        was then redelivered and reprinted verbatim on the next poll
        cycle, the same "risking a duplicate reply to an already-
        answered message" symptom TGT-132's own docs describe, just
        via a different unguarded call site. Both call sites now catch
        the error, print a STORE ERROR line to STDERR, and skip that
        one update non-fatally - the rest of the batch (and its own
        correct final offset) still completes normally.

1.32  2026-09-10
      - BUG FIX (TGT-164, found via a scheduled bug hunt): D2TG_CHAT_ID's
        canonical-shape validation (TGT-155's require_chat_id_or_warn)
        was only ever called when the CLI did NOT declare its own
        --chat_id group. Whenever cli/poller.pl's multi-bot CLI
        support (TGT-049) was used (e.g. `d2 tg.poller --chat_id 999
        --bot TOKEN`), the startup guard was skipped entirely -
        D2TG::Config::bot_groups' second call still silently folded a
        SET but malformed D2TG_CHAT_ID in as an additional implicit
        poll group, with no shape validation at all, instead of being
        refused the way the plain env-only path already refuses it.
        The env-folded value now runs through the same
        require_chat_id_or_warn check whenever D2TG_CHAT_ID is
        actually set (a merely unset env var alongside CLI groups is
        unaffected - bot_groups simply won't fold anything in for
        that case). CLI-declared --chat_id groups' own values remain
        unvalidated by this fix, unchanged - a CLI-declared chat_id is
        caller-supplied and outside this env-var validation, not an env
        leak. An empty-but-set D2TG_CHAT_ID is deliberately not refused
        by this guard either, matching bot_groups' own env-folding
        condition exactly - an empty string is never folded in as a
        group, so there is nothing for this guard to prevent there.

