1.28  2026-09-10
      - RELIABILITY FIX (TGT-160, found via scheduled hourly bug hunt
        JOB-003): D2TG::Config::is_transient_error never classified
        Telegram's own 429 ("Too Many Requests") rate-limit response as
        transient - only /timed out/i and /status 5\d\d/ matched.
        Telegram's Bot API documents 429 as a designed, expected,
        retryable rate-limit condition (a response body containing
        parameters.retry_after), not a genuine application error, but
        it was previously logged loudly as a genuine POLL ERROR on the
        monitored tira.policy.bridge stream every time routine rate
        limiting kicked in. Now returns true for a 429, matching the
        same treatment 5xx/timeout errors already get - run_once_safe's
        own retry/backoff timing is unchanged, only the loud-vs-silent
        logging decision changes. Deliberately does not read/honor
        Telegram's own parameters.retry_after value (would require
        parsing the response body, out of scope for this narrow
        classification fix).

