1.16  2026-09-09
      - D2TG::Telegram/D2TG::Poller (TGT-143, live Telegram question
        from Michael: "the user can give a like or mark a message with
        emoji, is that something can be implement to pick this up"):
        message reactions are now detected and printed. get_updates now
        requests allowed_updates explicitly ([message, message_reaction]
        by default), since reactions are opt-in per the Bot API and
        Telegram's own docs warn that specifying allowed_updates at all
        restricts delivery to only the listed types - every type this
        project already relied on is preserved alongside the new one.
        A reaction add prints "NEW TG REACTION [chat_id] sender: <emoji>
        on message <id>", a removal prints "REACTION REMOVED [chat_id]
        sender: <emoji> on message <id>" - diffed by emoji set (Codex
        review caught that a naive "any non-empty new_reaction = add"
        check would mishandle a same-update swap, e.g. one emoji
        replaced by another). Detection/printing only, no reply action.
        Codex also caught missing sanitization on the sender/emoji
        before printing - both fixed.

1.15  2026-09-09
      - D2TG::Poller (TGT-142, live Telegram question answered by
        Michael: "use the origin name instead of user id"): a
        forwarded message now names its original sender alongside the
        forwarder ("<original> (forwarded by <forwarder>)") instead of
        just the forwarder - reads Telegram's own forward_origin field
        (already reaching the poller untouched, simply never read
        before). All 4 MessageOrigin types handled (user, hidden_user,
        chat, channel); the reply-context suffix gets the same fix.
        Codex review caught 2 real issues: a truthy check that would
        have treated a literal "0" display name as absent (fixed to a
        defined check), and missing sanitization coverage for a
        hostile origin name (fixed, new tests added).

1.14  2026-09-09
      - D2TG::Lock (TGT-141, external review finding live-reproduced by
        a sibling project, confirmed by Michael): the orphaned-poller
        warning now cross-checks a flagged PID's own D2TG_TOKEN (via
        /proc/<pid>/environ) before deciding how urgent to sound - a
        same-token match keeps the urgent WARNING framing, a different
        or unreadable token gets a reassuring NOTE naming the
        sibling-project explanation instead. Previously every
        poller-shaped process on the host was warned about identically,
        firing routinely for the single most common, entirely benign
        case (each sibling project's own distinct bot token, no real
        getUpdates collision). Never-kill, report-only design unchanged.

1.13  2026-09-09
      - SECURITY (TGT-146, found via scheduled hourly bug hunt JOB-003,
        a TGT-133 regression): cli/retry-download.pl's own RETRY OK
        success line printed the real local filesystem path of a
        retried download directly to stdout - a leak onto the target
        project's tira.policy.bridge (monitor-output), the exact class
        of leak TGT-133 closed everywhere else (D2TG::Poller's own
        media-download success path, cli/attachment.pl). Fixed: names
        the d2 tg.attachment fetch command instead, never the raw path.

1.12  2026-09-09
      - DOC ACCURACY (TGT-145, found via JOB-005's scheduled doc-accuracy
        hunt): README.md, docs/commands.md (x2), and docs/POLICIES.md
        (x2) still described D2TG::Transcribe's scaled timeout as
        floored at a fixed 300s and capped at a fixed 3600s - stale
        since TGT-140's own QA-stage fix made both dynamic (floored at
        $TIMEOUT itself, capped at max(3600, $TIMEOUT)). Only the
        module's own POD had been updated at the time; the other 5
        prose locations drifted. Corrected to match the shipped code.

1.11  2026-09-09
      - D2TG::Config (TGT-139, self-review while completing TGT-138's
        pending-push gate): write_heartbeat's rename-failure path now
        unlinks its own staging temp file before dying - previously a
        failed rename() left $path.tmp.$$ behind, and every failed write
        attempt would add another orphaned file to the state directory.
        New optional renamer coderef for test injection, mirroring
        D2TG::TTS::synthesize_to_file's own pattern.

1.10  2026-09-09
      - D2TG::Transcribe (TGT-140, external review finding confirmed live
        by Michael): the hard whisper timeout now scales with the same
        duration signal select_model already computes, instead of staying
        a flat 300s constant - a clip on its selected tier's own real
        throughput (measured: medium ran at ~5.6x real time, a 102.48s
        clip took 571s) is no longer killed purely for exceeding the old
        flat ceiling. Floored at the original 300s (never worse than
        before) and capped at 3600s (never unbounded). Only applies to an
        automatically-selected model; an explicitly-passed model keeps the
        flat timeout unchanged, matching the retry-on-timeout fallback's
        own explicit-means-explicit scope.

