        docs/commands.md for "HTTP request failed (status 401
        Unauthorized)" - confirmed (side-by-side curl getMe + cli/poller
        in a developer-dashboard:latest container) this always means the
        configured D2TG_TOKEN is rejected by Telegram directly, not a
        code bug.

0.07  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-028, live production incident): cli/poller's loop
        had no error handling around D2TG::Poller::run_once - any
        transient getUpdates failure (a real one hit in production: 599
        Internal Exception, a low-level connection failure) propagated
        uncaught and silently killed the whole poller process, which
        then never fetched again until manually restarted. Fixed:
        D2TG::Poller::run_once_safe wraps run_once, logging POLL ERROR
        to stderr and retrying after a short backoff instead of dying.
      - D2TG::Telegram and D2TG::Download now use LWP::UserAgent instead
        of HTTP::Tiny (owner-directed, TGT-028) - cpanfile gained
        LWP::UserAgent as a new dependency.
      - BUGFIX found while verifying TGT-028's own fix: cli/poller never
        set $|=1 (autoflush). Previously this didn't matter because any
        transient failure crashed the process, which flushes all
        filehandles on exit; now that run_once_safe keeps the process
        alive through failures, STDOUT could sit block-buffered
        indefinitely instead of reaching the watched stream in real
        time. Fixed with an explicit $|=1.

0.08  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-027, found via IMPROVEMENT HUNT): cli/reply did not
        validate chat_id was numeric before use, unlike cli/approve.
        A non-numeric first argument silently reached D2TG::Telegram and
        failed there with an opaque error instead of a clean local
        Usage message. Fixed: cli/reply now uses the same /^-?\d+$/
        guard as cli/approve, exiting 2 with a Usage message on STDERR
        for a non-numeric chat_id, before any Telegram call is attempted.

0.09  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-031, live production incident, root-caused via direct
        process inspection): D2TG::Transcribe::_run's system(@cmd) call
        to whisper was fully blocking with no timeout - one slow voice
        transcription blocked the entire poll loop (no new messages of
        any kind fetched) and made the poller unresponsive to Ctrl+C/
        SIGTERM for as long as it ran, since Perl defers signal handling
        until a blocking syscall returns. Fixed: _run now forks and
        polls waitpid every 0.2s instead of blocking on it directly (so
        pending signals get a chance to run), enforces a configurable
        $TIMEOUT (default 300s) that kills the child and reports a
        normal TRANSCRIBE ERROR instead of blocking forever, and
        cli/poller's SIGTERM/SIGINT handlers now call the new
        D2TG::Transcribe::kill_current to end an in-flight transcription
        immediately at shutdown time.

0.10  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-030, live reproduction: Michael sent a voice
        message): whisper's own console output (FP16/CPU warning,
        language-detection lines, raw per-segment transcript lines) was
        inherited straight onto the poller's real stdout, polluting the
        watched NEW TG stream. Fixed: D2TG::Transcribe::_run's forked
        child now reopens its own STDOUT/STDERR onto /dev/null before
        exec - only this project's own structured lines ever reach the
        real stream.

0.11  2026-09-07
      - FEATURE (TGT-029, live usability report): the poller's NEW TG/
        NEW TG VOICE/NEW TG MEDIA lines now carry a "(replying to
        <sender>: <snippet-or-kind>)" suffix when Telegram's
        reply_to_message field is present, naming what a reply targets -
        previously a reply looked identical to a fresh message on
        stdout, giving the monitoring agent no way to tell which prior
        message in a conversation a reply responds to.

0.12  2026-09-07
      - DOCS (TGT-032): added a Troubleshooting entry for "HTTP request
        failed (status 409 Conflict)" - non-fatal (handled by
        run_once_safe/TGT-028), likely caused by a forced (non-clean)
        poller restart, now less likely since TGT-031's prompt-shutdown
        fix.

0.13  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-033, found while investigating TGT-030): D2TG::TTS::
        _run had the identical unredirected system(@cmd) pattern as
        D2TG::Transcribe's (fixed in TGT-030) - gtts-cli/ffmpeg's own
        console output could leak onto d2 tg.reply's stdout/stderr.
        Fixed with the same shape: STDOUT/STDERR are temporarily
        redirected to /dev/null around the system() call and restored
        immediately after.

0.14  2026-09-07
      - REFACTOR (TGT-034, found via IMPROVEMENT HUNT): t/23 and t/25's
        near-identical FD save/redirect/restore/compare boilerplate
        extracted into a shared t/lib/Test/CaptureStdio.pm helper
        (capture_stdio), matching the same test-infra deduplication
        pattern already applied once (TGT-018). No behavior change -
        all existing assertions in both files pass unchanged.

0.15  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-035, live E2E screen recording, 3 problems found and
        fixed): (1) D2TG::Telegram's default LWP::UserAgent had no
        explicit timeout, defaulting to LWP's own 180s - Ctrl+C/SIGTERM
        could still be delayed up to 180s even after TGT-031's
        transcription-timeout fix, since Perl defers signal handling
        until the current blocking get_updates HTTP call returns. Fixed
        with an explicit timeout => 35 (a few seconds above
        get_updates' own 30s server-side hint), genuinely bounding both
        shutdown delay and new-message latency to ~35s. (2)
        D2TG::Poller::_reply_context_suffix's 60-char truncation was far
        too aggressive to be useful context for a real conversation -
        raised to 5000 chars, comfortably exceeding Telegram's own
        4096-char message limit so a quoted message is effectively
        never truncated. (3) A message that appeared to "vanish"
        (no reply-context notification ever appeared for a genuine
        Telegram reply) was very likely caused by the same root cause
        as (1) - the poller's current poll cycle was still blocked and
        had not reached the next cycle to fetch it.

0.16  2026-09-07
      - FEATURE (TGT-036, owner request): the poller now self-refreshes
        when a newer version is installed while it's already running.
        D2TG::Config::skill_version reads the installed VERSION from
        .env; after each poll cycle cli/poller compares it to the
        version it started with, and if it changed, cleanly disconnects
        D2TG::Store's DB handle (new disconnect method) and re-execs
        itself in place (same PID) - a fresh Perl interpreter then loads
        the newly-installed code. A pending shutdown always takes
        priority over a detected version change.

0.17  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-037, live bug report): a large photo/document
        produced an unexplained "MEDIA DOWNLOAD ERROR ... HTTP request
        failed (status 400 Bad Request)" - Telegram's Bot API getFile
        endpoint has a hard, documented 20MB limit. D2TG::Poller now
        checks the message's own declared file_size before attempting a
        download; a file over 20MB is reported with a specific "file
        too large to download" error naming the limit, and the doomed
        getFile call is never attempted at all. Normal-sized files are
        unaffected.

0.18  2026-09-07
      - FEATURE (TGT-038, live design proposal from Michael): a reply to
        an uploaded photo/document previously showed only the bare media
        kind ("document"/"photo") in its reply-context suffix, with no
        way to tell which one. D2TG::Store gains a messages table plus
        record_message/get_message; D2TG::Poller now records a short
        summary of every successfully processed message (its text, its
        transcript for voice, or "<kind> <local_path>" for a downloaded
        photo/document) against that message's own chat_id+message_id.
        _reply_context_suffix looks up the replied-to message's stored
        summary first; only when nothing was ever stored for it (predates
        this feature, or the sender was never allow-listed at the time)
        does it fall back to the original Telegram-payload-only
        behavior, unchanged.

0.19  2026-09-07
      - BUGFIX (TGT-039, code-review bug hunt finding): a voice
        transcript could legitimately contain embedded newlines (whisper
        emits one line per segment), and unlike text messages it was
        printed/stored raw - breaking the single-line-per-event stdout
        contract the whole architecture (Tira monitor job feeder) relies
        on. D2TG::Poller's text-branch sanitization (newline -> literal
        \n, strip other control chars) is now extracted into
        _sanitize_for_stdout and applied to the voice-transcript branch
        too, before both printing and storing (TGT-038's record_message).

0.20  2026-09-07
      - FEATURE (TGT-040, live follow-up question - "where is the message
        id?"): every content line (NEW TG / NEW TG VOICE / NEW TG MEDIA)
        and the REPLY WITH template now name the inbound message's own
        message_id. D2TG::Telegram::send_message/send_voice gain an
        optional reply_to_message_id; D2TG::Reply::send_reply and
        cli/reply (new --reply-to-message-id flag) thread it through, so
        a reply can now be sent as a genuine Telegram-native reply -
        threaded under the original message in Telegram's UI - instead
        of always arriving as a fresh, unthreaded message. Omitting the
