0.67  2026-09-08
      - FIX (TGT-091, live production incident - Michael's zen-framework
        project): TIRA_HOME's value is now resolved against the d2 paths
        table first, exactly like an explicit --db/-d/D2TG_DB alias,
        falling back to treating it as a literal filesystem path only
        if it matches no registered alias. TGT-090 (shipped moments
        earlier) exposed this: TIRA_HOME=tira-zen - a real, registered
        alias resolving to /home/mv/.tira/zenandi - was being treated
        as a literal path and correctly rejected as nonexistent by
        TGT-090's new check, blocking d2 tg.poller from starting at all
        in zen-framework. TGT-090's fix itself was correct and is
        unchanged; this closes the gap one level up, in how TIRA_HOME
        itself gets interpreted.

0.68  2026-09-08
      - FIX (TGT-092, live production incident): a photo/document
        message's caption was never captured or printed at all -
        Telegram's Bot API attaches it as a field separate from the
        plain-text $message->{text}, and the poller silently dropped it.
        Michael sent a photo with a caption describing a real problem to
        solve, and it never reached stdout/the bridge, causing a genuine
        miscommunication. A present caption is now sanitized the same
        way inbound text already is (TGT-039) and appended to both the
        printed NEW TG MEDIA line and the stored message summary; a
        message with no caption (the common case) is unaffected.

0.69  2026-09-08
      - CHANGE (TGT-093, live user request via Telegram): every cli/*
