        `text` column needed the same `ALTER TABLE`-with-duplicate-
        tolerance migration pattern `messages.read_at` already uses - a
        bare `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` is a no-op against a database
        that already has `sent_replies` from an earlier TGT-105-only
        install. Also fixed: `window_seconds` now rejects negative/
        non-numeric values. Three further findings (no protection
        against an ambiguous `send_message` failure, no atomicity under
        genuine concurrency, second-granular timing) were confirmed
        real but accepted as documented limitations, matching this
        project's own established practice for this class of tradeoff.

